=== Three quantitative statements suitable for the paper ===
  (1) Within-disease concordance is strongest for inflammatory bowel disease, rho = +0.1174; the two weakest disorders
      have observed values of +0.0026 and -0.0089, while their critical values are 0.0163 and 0.0274 -
      the test itself is sensitive enough; there is simply no reproducible signal.
  (2) The observed value of inflammatory bowel disease is 7.2 times the critical value of Alzheimer's disease; a reproducible signal
      of that order in the latter would certainly be detected by this design.
  (3) The highest of the forty cross-disease cells is +0.0484 (schizophrenia-depression: GSE80417 vs GSE273970); relative to the weakest within-disease value
      (+0.0430) it is of the same order. But it is only one of the four pairings of that disease pair, and the other three are -0.013, -0.009, +0.032;
      none of the ten disease pairs is significant in all four cohort pairings. The point is not how high a single cell is 
      but whether the four pairings agree - looking at the highest cell alone would lead to the opposite conclusion.

=== Effective number of independent probes (a note for the Methods, not a finding) ===
  Back-calculated from the SD of the null (1 over the variance); a heuristic quantity: the SD of the correlation between two independent random vectors
  is about 1 over the square root of the number of probes, which can be inverted to estimate 'how many
  independent probes this corresponds to'. It explains why detection limits differ so much between pairs, but removing it changes no conclusion, 
  so it belongs in the Methods only and is not a finding.
  highest  37492 (Parkinson|Depression), lowest    505 (Depression|IBD), median   2461
  Meaning: the detection limit depends on how much independent information remains given the residual correlation structure, not on the total number of probes.

